// `--json` writes each diagnostic as a JSON object on a line of standard error, with where
// it ends as well as where it starts, and its notes, each a place and a message; a summary
// record comes last. The text form has the same: a note is a line under its error.
//# $ ctxc check --json {dir}/a.ctx
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {"type":"diagnostic","severity":"error","file":"{dir}/a.ctx","line":9,"column":17,"end_line":9,"end_column":20,"message":"literal 300 does not fit in u8","notes":[]}
//| {"type":"diagnostic","severity":"error","file":"{dir}/a.ctx","line":4,"column":5,"end_line":4,"end_column":14,"message":"returned value holds the address of local `v`","notes":[{"file":"{dir}/a.ctx","line":3,"column":5,"end_line":3,"end_column":19,"message":"`v` is declared here"}]}
//| {"type":"diagnostic","severity":"error","file":"{dir}/a.ctx","line":8,"column":5,"end_line":8,"end_column":15,"message":"cannot store the address of local `n` in `box`, which belongs to the caller","notes":[{"file":"{dir}/a.ctx","line":7,"column":5,"end_line":7,"end_column":19,"message":"`n` is declared here"},{"file":"{dir}/a.ctx","line":6,"column":11,"end_line":6,"end_column":23,"message":"`box` is a context field, declared here"}]}
//| {"type":"summary","errors":3,"more":false,"waiting":["order","tasks","consts"]}
//# $ ctxc check {dir}/a.ctx
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/a.ctx:9:17: error: literal 300 does not fit in u8
//| {dir}/a.ctx:4:5: error: returned value holds the address of local `v`
//|   {dir}/a.ctx:3:5: note: `v` is declared here
//| {dir}/a.ctx:8:5: error: cannot store the address of local `n` in `box`, which belongs to the caller
//|   {dir}/a.ctx:7:5: note: `n` is declared here
//|   {dir}/a.ctx:6:11: note: `box` is a context field, declared here
//| check: 3 errors; not checked until the program has no other error: the order of a call's fields, what tasks borrow, consts computed by running code

// A program without errors has the summary alone. `--json` may come after the path.
//# $ ctxc check {dir}/ok.ctx --json
//# stderr:
//| {"type":"summary","errors":0,"more":false,"waiting":[]}

// The checks that waited are named, as the text form's last line names them: here the
// consts computed by running code, behind an error in the order of a call's fields.
//# $ ctxc check --json {dir}/order.ctx
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {"type":"diagnostic","severity":"error","file":"{dir}/order.ctx","line":8,"column":27,"end_line":8,"end_column":41,"message":"`n` reads `s.n`, which `z` changes, in one call: the order of the fields would decide what it reads; compute one of them in a `let` before the call","notes":[{"file":"{dir}/order.ctx","line":8,"column":22,"end_line":8,"end_column":25,"message":"`n` reads `s.n` here"},{"file":"{dir}/order.ctx","line":8,"column":37,"end_line":8,"end_column":39,"message":"`z` changes `s.n` here"}]}
//| {"type":"summary","errors":1,"more":false,"waiting":["consts"]}

// A file that can't be read is the driver's failure, not a diagnostic: its line is text, and
// no summary follows.
//# $ ctxc check --json {dir}/missing.ctx
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| {dir}/missing.ctx: cannot read
